-- title:
--   A one-sided pool of étale blocks in the smooth locus
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, the hypothesis $hj$ that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion function field of level $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and a model bundle $\mathfrak{X}$ of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Assume given: an $R p$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin` such that $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.w.\mathrm{hom}$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\theta$ followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$, and such that $\mathfrak{X}.w.\mathrm{hom}$ pulls the open range of $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ back to itself; an element $f \in R p$ and an element $v$ of the chart algebra; a dictionary hypothesis stating that for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, every ring map $\rho : R p \to A$ compatible with $R p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every point $y$ of the fibre of `toBase` along the residue composite of $\rho$, and every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of the chart algebra with $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathfrak{q})$ the image of $y$ under the first projection, the condition $v \notin \mathfrak{q}$ forces $y$ to lie in the range of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,\rho\,0$ and off the range of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,\rho\,1$; and level-polynomial data consisting of $b, N_1 \in \mathbb{N}$, monic $g_i \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ and ranks $r_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,N_1$) such that each quotient of the chart algebra by the ideal generated by $g_i(v)$ is a finite, étale, free $R p$-module of rank $r_i$ with $1 \le r_i \le b$, the ideals $(g_i(v))$ are pairwise comaximal, $(g_i(v)) + (g_j(\theta v)) = (1)$ for all $i,j$, and $(g_i(v)) + (v) = (1)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring $R'$, finite, étale and faithfully flat over $\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f$ and an $R p$-algebra in a scalar tower, of rings $B_i$ finite étale over $\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f$, of integers $\mathrm{deg}_i$ with $1 \le \mathrm{deg}_i \le b$ together with $R'$-algebra isomorphisms $R' \otimes B_i \cong \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{deg}_i) \to R'$, and of closed immersions $z_i : \mathrm{Spec}\,B_i \to$ the base change of `toBase` along $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f) \to \mathrm{Spec}(R p)$, such that: $z_i$ followed by the base-changed structure morphism is $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f \to B_i$; the range of each $z_i$ lies in the preimage of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$ under the first projection; the ranges of the $z_i$ are pairwise disjoint; for every algebraically closed field $k$, every $s : \mathrm{Spec}\,k \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f)$ and every $i$, the preimage of the range of $z_i$ in the fibre over $s$ is contained in the connected component, inside the preimage of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$, of the point cut out by the base change of the section $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ at the closed point of $k$; the range of each $z_i$ is disjoint from the ranges of the base-changed sections $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{0}$; and the range of each $z_i$ is disjoint from the range of $z_j$ followed by the base change of $\mathfrak{X}.w.\mathrm{hom}$, for all $i,j$.
--
--   This produces, from level-polynomial data on the $j$-finite chart, a single family ("one-sided pool") of finite étale closed blocks in the smooth locus of the $\Gamma_H$-model over $R p$ localised away from $f$, mutually disjoint and disjoint from the two marked sections and from the $\mathfrak{X}.w$-image of the family, all geometric fibres of the blocks lying in the connected component of the $\varepsilon_{\inf}$-point; the splitting of the blocks is achieved after a finite étale faithfully flat extension $R'$. It feeds the constructions of two-sided pools in the smooth locus at the closed primes $2$, $3$ and $\ge 5$ under a genericity assumption on the Atkin–Lehner involution.
